  "data": {
    "body": "Which of the following statements are/is true?\n\n\n\n(i) An $n \\times n$ matrix that is orthogonally diagonalized must be symmetric.\n\n(ii) An $n \\times n$ symmetric matrix has $n$ distinct real eigenvalues.\n\n(iii) There are symmetric matrices that are not orthogonally diagonalizable.\n\n(iv) If $B=P D P^{T}$, where $P^{T}=P^{-1}$ and $D$ is a diagonal matrix, then $B$ is a symmetric matrix.",
